a.record('pfp/domain/normal_forms/relational.py',221,1027,'Completed body: FD chase globally merges symbols and preserves BudgetUnknown on exhaustion, with finite countermodel tableau after saturation. Out-of-heading determinant attributes are silently dropped, potentially turning a dependency unconditional. Keys supplied to chase are premises, not inferred there. RFNF/6NF/DKNF explicitly retain screen/declared-theory limits, while other forms enumerate only supplied JDs/MVDs. Minimal cover and exhaustive projected FDs implement useful finite closure algebra. 5NF synthesis invents an unsupported cyclic-key JD and may return lossy projections; pruning checks do not establish the original decomposition. A zero/single-component lossless call returns true without heading coverage. Relation evaluator uses finite set semantics, missing values as None and hashable values. Confluence enumerates supplied/all FD orders with factorial growth and does not distinguish equal budget-unknown outcomes from saturated proofs. Candidate and closure algorithms have exponential input growth without budgets.')
a.record('pfp/domain/normal_forms/relational_extensions.py',1,503,'MVD chase combines finite symbol merges and tuple synthesis but lacks heading-union validation, clips dependency attributes and conflates budget exhaustion with false implication. At budget one it skips FD phase entirely; at larger budgets inner FD fixpoint does not consume iteration allowance. Row growth is unbounded beyond finite implicit symbol carrier. 4NF checks supplied MVDs plus BCNF, assuming complete valid dependency theory. Closure axioms are exhaustively tested on finite subsets, but Kuratowski topological union preservation is not checked and generally does not hold. Candidate antichain is recomputation, not independent evidence. ZFNF scaling calls the weak scalar-only certifier. Simplicial helper derives d0/d1 with orientation correctly for valid carrier, but no carrier validation or harmonic-kernel test; it checks orthogonality to one supplied gradient, not every gradient.')
a.record('pfp/domain/normal_forms/relational_advanced.py',1,303,'GYO removes contained edges and ears whose shared vertices fit another edge; finite acyclicity mechanism with explicit trace. Bernstein synthesis uses minimal cover, adds a key and removes contained components, conditional on valid heading/FD assumptions. BCNF recursion projects full FD closures, preserving lossless binary decomposition but not generally all dependencies. EKNF examines supplied basis and internally defined elementary keys; source references are labels, not independently verified literature equivalence. Nest/unnest preserves only selected columns and can overwrite colliding nested/group names. Temporal 6NF ignores temporal_key_attrs, takes one key plus each nonprime attribute, can drop prime attributes belonging to alternate keys, and merely equal-joins time values rather than interval overlap. A key-plus-one-attribute shape does not prove 6NF under all join dependencies.')
