rows=[
(43,'Adjacent normal-form registry rejects its own nine-entry YAML','The strict index requires ten exact contract IDs including nf.experimental.qm_classical, but the adjacent YAML declares nine and omits that ID. Validation of the exact parsed YAML fails the complete-canonical-set check. The alternate types registry requires nine, leaving callers with incompatible contracts.',[ev('nf_domain_index.py',(29,42),(85,100)),ev('nf_domain_index.yaml',(1,59))],[52]),
(44,'BQNF certified repairs omit group and predicate effects','Moving amount 10 from group A to B yields certified new-group delta zero, rather than A minus 10/B plus 10. AVG inserts an unpaid row despite status = paid predicate. The evaluator accepts these boundary declarations yet ignores group relocation and AVG filtering; certified true overstates the finite update semantics.',[ev('bqnf_validator.py',(208,245),(258,304))],[54]),
(45,'Finite meron cancellation admits negative survivors and overwritten sectors','MIC converts sectors into a dictionary without duplicate-ID rejection and does not require nonnegative magnitudes. A single sign +1, weight -1 row returns MeronExactCancellation with survivor sum -1. Duplicate IDs silently change the original signed sum, so declared table preservation is not established.',[ev('quantum_forms.py',(230,293),(324,335))],[55]),
(46,'Simplex verifier accepts edges outside its vertex carrier','TSNF builds a zero edge boundary when either endpoint is absent but records no defect. Vertices [0] with edge (1,2) is accepted as TSNF with b1=1. Nilpotency and the algebraically dependent Euler check cannot substitute for closure of the supplied simplicial carrier.',[ev('topology.py',(152,200),(305,372))],[57]),
(47,'Zero-gap verifier does not bind feasibility or objective values','ZFNF defaults absent feasibility to true and never recomputes objective scalars from witnesses. Scalars 7/7 alone yield CertifiedOptimalZeroGap; feasible witnesses with actual objectives 1/1 also certify claimed 999/999. Equal scalars are insufficient to establish optimality of a bound problem.',[ev('tower_forms.py',(101,150),(153,196))],[59]),
(48,'Hodge exactness accepts a non-gradient labelled vector','DHNF checks reconstruction and pairwise orthogonality of supplied vectors, but never tests whether d0_p belongs to a coboundary image or h to a harmonic kernel. A triangle vector with circulation 3 assigned wholly to d0_p yields HodgeDecomposedExact, although every vertex gradient has circulation zero.',[ev('tower_forms.py',(209,245))],[60]),
(49,'Reconciliation authorizes an unauthenticated verifier label and unsealed loss ledger','An outcome=verified dictionary is treated as an authenticated target verifier. A ledger containing only erased_attributes passes integrity with no entries or digest. Together these yield certified and authorized true for an empty quotient projection. This is a domain return value; no external authorization operation was exercised.',[ev('reconciliation.py',(146,180),(207,278),(308,363))],[61]),
(50,'Account and currency concatenation aliases distinct reconciliation keys','Reconciliation uses account_id + colon + currency as a product key without escaping or type restrictions. Source pair (a:b,c) and target pair (a,b:c) both map to a:b:c, so equal amounts across different accounts/currencies reconcile and authorize.',[ev('reconciliation.py',(281,305),(308,363))],[62]),
(51,'5NF projection synthesis invents a lossy cyclic-key decomposition','With candidate keys AB, AC and BC and no declared join dependency, synthesis returns those pair projections precisely when keys do not imply their join. The four even-parity binary triples satisfy all three keys, yet their projections join to eight rows. Cyclic keys alone do not justify the generated lossless-reconstruction claim.',[ev('relational.py',(767,841),(870,897))],[64]),
(52,'Relational validators omit heading and single-projection coverage checks','FD chase drops determinant attributes outside the heading, turning Z→B on heading AB into an unconditional merge and accepting the A/B decomposition. check_lossless_decomposition separately accepts a lone projection A of heading AB without checking coverage. Invalid inputs should not receive a mathematical losslessness verdict.',[ev('relational.py',(314,349),(371,394),(972,987))],[65]),
(53,'MVD chase turns exhausted work into non-implication','For heading ABC, decomposition AB/BC and FD B→C, max_iterations=1 skips the FD phase and returns is_implied false; budget two returns true. The result has no unknown/status alternative. This differs from the FD-only chase, which preserves BudgetUnknown for zero budget.',[ev('relational_extensions.py',(238,273),(294,307)),ev('relational.py',(472,503))],[66]),
(54,'Temporal decomposition drops alternate-key attributes','Given heading ABCD with keys A and B and nonprime C,D, temporal_6nf_decompose returns AC and AD, losing B. temporal_key_attrs is unused. The returned schemas are therefore not even a covering decomposition, before any claimed 6NF or interval semantics are assessed.',[ev('relational_advanced.py',(262,303))],[67])]
